<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bonds ended higher in line with other markets on Friday but traders said volume was light and the market was beginning to wind down ahead of Holy Week.</p>
<p>With little domestic news to feed from, traders said the market had limited itself to following in the wake of other bonds.</p>
<p>Dealers said although they feared an interest rate hike at the U.S. FOMC meeting next Tuesday, the possibility had already largely been factored into the market.</p>
</text>
